      "message": "From discussion in chat:\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\n\nI think there may be a bug in LocalSocketImpl#read_native?\n\nthe stack trace suggests the code is calling jniThrowIOException when an exception has already been thrown\nmaybe it\u0027s here?\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/frameworks/base/core/jni/android_net_LocalSocketImpl.cpp;l\u003d257\n\n    err \u003d socket_read_all(env, object, fd, \u0026buf, 1);\n\n    if (err \u003c 0) {\n        jniThrowIOException(env, errno);\n        return (jint)0;\n    }\n\nif socket_read_all has already thrown when it returns a negative result, then jniThrowIOException must not be called\nand in fact, it has already thrown:\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/frameworks/base/core/jni/android_net_LocalSocketImpl.cpp;l\u003d143\n\njniThrowIOException(env, errno);\n        return -1;\n\nso I think you  need:\nsomething like:\n\n    if (err \u003c 0) {\n-       jniThrowIOException(env, errno);\n+       // socket_read_all has already thrown\n        return (jint)0;\n    }\n\n",
